agbcp/old_agbcp: agbcc's compiler switches in the C++ compiler
==============================================================

Applies to notyourav/agbcc's `cp` branch (its g++/ tree: gcc
2.9-arm-000512 with the C++ front end, whose cc1plus is decomp.me's
"agbccpp") with `patch -p1` from the checkout's root.
tools/build_agbccpp.sh does that on a copy and builds it twice: as
tools/agbcc/bin/agbcp, and with -DOLD_COMPILER as .../old_agbcp.

Why: SAT-R/agbcc builds agbcc and old_agbcc from one gcc/ tree, the
latter with -DOLD_COMPILER, and agbcc has -fprologue-bugfix. The `cp`
branch's g++/ tree is the same compiler without either, so its cc1plus
generates agbcc's code minus the prologue bugfix, and can't generate
old_agbcc's. This patch ports both (docs/cplusplus.md):

  -fprologue-bugfix   toplev.c, flags.h, config/arm/thumb.c: the option,
                      which makes far_jump_used_p rescan instead of
                      trusting its cached answer (the "lr saved for no
                      reason" bug). The Makefile passes it to agbcp as
                      it does to agbcc.

  -DOLD_COMPILER      config/arm/thumb.c: s_register_operand is plain
                      register_operand (this is what gives old_agbcc's
                      constant-before-`ldrb` scheduling), and
                      far_jump_used_p never caches.
                      function.c: no use_return_register () at the end
                      of a function.
                      loop.c: check_dbra_loop doesn't check that the biv
                      increment is a CONST_INT.
                      unroll.c: local_regno is bounded by maxregnum.

  -fhex-asm fix       config/arm/thumb.c: the epilogue of a function with
                      pretend (stdarg) arguments printed `add sp, sp,
                      0x<decimal>`, which doesn't assemble. SAT-R/agbcc
                      prints `#0x<hex>`; so does this.

Without -DOLD_COMPILER and -fprologue-bugfix the patched compiler is
the stock one, apart from that fix.

